{"id": "EUVD-2026-102342", "enisaUuid": "99d9adb8-d3c1-3ea0-ae5a-dbfcdf9767b4", "description": "Netgate pfSense CE through 2.9.0 contains a local file read vulnerability that allows users with the Dynamic DNS client privilege to read files as root by setting a file:// custom Update URL in services_dyndns_edit.php. Attackers can set a non-matching Result Match string so _checkStatus() logs file contents such as /conf/config.xml or /etc/master.passwd to the system log.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:46:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:48:31", "baseScore": 6.9, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/abraxas/pfsense-dyndns-file", "https://abraxaslabs.tech/research/pfsense-ce-leftovers", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/dyndns.class#L598-L616", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/etc/inc/dyndns.class#L2151-L2171", "https://github.com/pfsense/pfsense/blob/9363ac5b8651a1c7a333180425ce7719070f95f9/src/usr/local/www/services_dyndns_edit.php#L138-L141", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/netgate-pfsense-ce-through-2.9.0-local-file-read-via-dynamic-dns-update-url"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111230", "GHSA-c3v6-7g6h-r7q8"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.75, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "48c4c023-93e9-3d4e-8c9f-bdd77c4807cf", "product": {"name": "pfSense CE", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.9.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0e6becfe-d978-372c-aaba-143dfb684cee", "vendor": {"name": "Netgate"}}], "isExploited": false}